    <string name="cue_neh_sol_1">Feed your baby</string>
    <string name="cue_neh_sol_2">Don’t interrupt your baby’s feeding time</string>
    <string name="cue_neh_sol_3">Don’t try to burp them while she/ he is in the middle of the feeding activities</string>
    <string name="cue_neh_sol_4">Leave them feed to the full duration they are willing to, unless they’re saying the other word like \"Eh\" in the middle of the feeding process</string>
    <string name="cue_owh_sol_1">Help your baby fall asleep</string>
    <string name="cue_owh_sol_2">If your baby is particularly windy, they are probably prefer to go sleep in upright position</string>
    <string name="cue_owh_sol_3">Make sure your baby has been burped, so your baby can fall asleep much more easily</string>
    <string name="cue_owh_sol_4">Nothing better than rocking your baby to sleep, it’s a wonderful time to help with the bonding process</string>
    <string name="cue_eh_sol_1">Burp your baby</string>
    <string name="cue_eh_sol_2">You’ll may find that your baby is need to be burped throughout the day, not only after feed</string>
    <string name="cue_eh_sol_3">If your baby says the word \"Eh\" before feed, you definitely need to burp your baby first, don’t feed the baby who needs to be burped</string>
    <string name="cue_eh_sol_4">Just because you hear a loud burp, doesn’t means that the air bubbles has been removed, you will know that when your baby stop saying the word \"Eh\"</string>
    <string name="cue_eh_sol_5">If your baby is sleeping when you hear the word \"Eh\", try to burping them first and then putting them back to sleep to finish their nap</string>
    <string name="cue_eh_sol_6">When you wrapped a child with a windy problem, best to wrapped them tightly around their tummy, but free their legs and one arm so they can movethem when necessary.</string>
    <string name="cue_eairh_sol_1">Use massage and lower wind holds, the one of settling technique is cross your legs, place your baby’s stomach into your thigh and rock, try to apply pressure with your knee on your baby’s lower stomach</string>
    <string name="cue_eairh_sol_2">The other method is put your baby on your shoulder, hold on tight or try to walk around with your baby over your arm</string>
    <string name="cue_eairh_sol_3">Put your baby on their stomach and rub their back is also helping</string>
    <string name="cue_eairh_sol_4">Massaging your baby’s stomach helps to move air bubbles</string>
    <string name="cue_eairh_sol_5">Always burp your baby when they says the word \"Eh\" to prevent the air bubbles go lower</string>
    <string name="cue_eairh_sol_6">Don’t ever put your baby to sleep when they are saying the word \"Eairh\"</string>
    <string name="cue_heh_sol_1">If the baby feels too hot, you can remove some clothes or his bedding, if it’s too cold you may need to add them</string>
    <string name="cue_heh_sol_2">If wet, change the diaper</string>
    <string name="cue_heh_sol_3">Try to pick your baby up and change their position</string>
